  "raw": " being possessed.\n\nThe police chief is Terrence Mellody (Zach McGowan) who looks like he has just arrived from jail. He is one of those cops that sucks at investigating. Known for early retirement, and for going rogue in the past. Everybody knows his name among the demons because of a massacre that he committed many years ago.\n\nHe doesn’t tell Jared (Matthew Lederer) about his investigation in exchange for loyalty but Gravestone (Kyle MacLachlan) sees through this. He told Jeremy (Yeardley Smith) everything, including the fact that this makes it simple for prosecutors to accuse Justin (Samuel West), who had been presumed innocent until proven guilty. That was not the same case anymore and now the damnable creatures and their teams cannot do anything else other than watch as justice takes its inevitable trip through hellhole found inside of a prison. Now, if only Liam could help him out anytime soon?",
  "serialized": "being possessed. The police chief is Terrence Mellody (Zach McGowan) who looks like he has just arrived from jail. He is one of those cops that sucks at investigating. Known for early retirement, and for going rogue in the past. Everybody knows his name among the demons because of a massacre that he committed many years ago. He doesn’t tell Jared (Matthew Lederer) about his investigation in exchange for loyalty but Gravestone (Kyle MacLachlan) sees through this. He told Jeremy (Yeardley Smith) everything, including the fact that this makes it simple for prosecutors to accuse Justin (Samuel West), who had been presumed innocent until proven guilty. That was not the same case anymore and now the damnable creatures and their teams cannot do anything else other than watch as justice takes its inevitable trip through hellhole found inside of a prison. Now, if only Liam could help him out anytime soon?",
